                                                                                "take":  "This is Santoli at his most useful: not calling a top, but mapping the landmines. The earnings-concentration data is the most actionable piece ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â when two companies drive a third of index EPS growth, you are effectively running a concentrated portfolio inside an index wrapper. Equal-weight S\u0026P exposure (RSP) is a straightforward hedge against this concentration without abandoning equities. The complacency-plus-full-allocation combination is also the classic setup for outsized September volatility: no one is hedged, no one has cash, so when a catalyst hits, the exit is crowded. The alert is not to sell, but to ensure your portfolio can weather a 5-10% drawdown without forcing you to liquidate at the wrong time.",
